WEBVTT

00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:19,010
Having energy all day for different things, ATP and cells are working good.

00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:26,270
So if you have energy all day for different things, does that mean your cells are producing

00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:28,590
a lot of ATP?

00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:35,770
Yeah, I would say so, yeah, but there's other reasons why a person wouldn't have energy.

00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:43,210
So you can't just say because I have tired, I'm tired, my mitochondria don't produce

00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:44,210
ATP.

00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:45,210
That's why.

00:00:45,210 --> 00:00:47,210
So I really need to boost my mitochondria.

00:00:47,210 --> 00:00:49,930
No, you've got to look at why am I tired?

00:00:49,930 --> 00:00:52,010
Do I have anemia?

00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:54,210
Do I have a growth of cancer?

00:00:54,210 --> 00:00:57,090
If I had a cancer diagnosis, do I have something else serious going on?

00:00:57,090 --> 00:00:58,090
Do I have liver congestion?

00:00:58,090 --> 00:01:00,370
Do I have detoxification issues?

00:01:00,370 --> 00:01:03,610
Do I have, you know, there's food sensitivities and inflammation?

00:01:03,610 --> 00:01:09,650
There's just a lot of different reasons why a person would not have energy.

00:01:09,650 --> 00:01:14,810
But could you say because I have energy, my mitochondria are working well?

00:01:14,810 --> 00:01:21,650
Oh, I guess you could, you know, because I could walk up today and I could breathe, my lungs

00:01:21,650 --> 00:01:22,650
are functioning well.

00:01:22,650 --> 00:01:24,650
Does it mean they could be functioning better?

00:01:24,650 --> 00:01:26,770
Yeah, I don't know, but yes.

